  "interpretation": [
    "Original RC6 reproduced an internal omnibox renderer callback-buffer assertion twice; main browser survived both failures.",
    "Closed preloaded WebUI is now hidden at the View layer; the presenter reveals it before sizing and hides it on dismissal.",
    "Renderer-only RC3 still missed the repeated warm-switch gate at 52.266417 ms. The final helper removes redundant post-focus discovery and retains native focus synchronization.",
    "RC4 skipped native focus synchronization and lost startup selection; that optimization was removed.",
    "First RC5 35-page attempt completed mapping but its environment observer rejected target identity. No latency samples were collected; this invalid attempt is retained and excluded from the two accepted runs.",
    "Early autocomplete probe failures included dropped events from a short-lived sender; it now waits for delivery and verifies the typed query through Accessibility.",
    "Native video controls can auto-hide; the driver reveals controls with Tab and still requires a real exit-button Accessibility press.",
    "Helper production launch policy sets ThrottleInterval to two seconds; fixture copies that packaged policy and retains a ten-second budget."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Input latency includes command and probe observation overhead; not compositor presentation latency. Sequential 60-sample runs do not establish long-run population percentiles.",
    "Helper process-death checks use an observe-only helper and prove automatic transport/inventory recovery. Managed layout reply-loss is a separate test.",
    "Original whole-browser disappearance remains unreproduced. Authenticated Twitter/X video and native hang-stack capture remain unqualified.",
    "No long-duration, aged-profile, sleep/wake, multi-display or sustained memory-pressure qualification was performed.",
    "Existing unrelated native/sidebar working-tree changes are included in the signed package and fingerprinted; this is not an isolated helper A/B against the original RC6."
  ],
